# Local and legacy env files. These used to be committed, which meant every
# deployment shipped a file naming the OLD api host. Next loads .env.local and
# .env.production during a build, so they only lost to the per-slot file by
# precedence — one plain `next build` instead of `build:{env}:{country}` and
# the wrong API would be baked in silently.
.env.local
.env.production
.env.qa

# Per-slot environment files for the four storefront deployments.
#
# TEMPORARY (2026-09-14): tracked so config changes can be shipped through
# git during pre-launch testing. Every secret currently in these files
# must be ROTATED before public launch — git history preserves the
# values in perpetuity, so any credential ever committed here is
# considered burned for post-launch use.
#
# .env.prod.ca   — TRACKED (pre-launch); rotate secrets before launch
# .env.prod.us   — TRACKED (pre-launch); rotate secrets before launch
# .env.qa.ca     — TRACKED (pre-launch)
# .env.qa.us     — TRACKED (pre-launch)

# # env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
# .env.local
# .env.qa
# !.env.production

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
